description: Auth and password sign-in changes — load domain memory first
globs: src/**/Auth*.tsx,src/lib/auth*.ts,src/pages/SignIn.tsx,src/pages/AuthCallback.tsx,src/features/auth/**,src/features/profile/ProfilePasswordSection.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

Before editing auth files, read [docs/memory-auth.md](docs/memory-auth.md) and [docs/decisions.md](docs/decisions.md) (2026-05-22 password auth).

## Screen → file map

| Task | Edit only |
| --- | --- |
| Sign-in form / forgot link | `src/features/auth/screens/SignInForm.tsx` |
| Create account form | `src/features/auth/screens/SignUpForm.tsx` |
| Forgot password form | `src/features/auth/screens/ForgotPasswordForm.tsx` |
| Post sign-up email sent | `src/features/auth/screens/ConfirmEmailSent.tsx` |
| Post reset email sent | `src/features/auth/screens/ResetEmailSent.tsx` |
| Choose new password (reset link) | `src/features/auth/screens/SetNewPasswordForm.tsx` |
| Screen routing / tab state | `src/features/auth/AuthPanel.tsx`, `src/features/auth/types.ts` |
| Shared email/password fields | `src/features/auth/components/*` |
| Supabase calls / validation / errors | `src/lib/authPassword.ts` |
| Redirects / recovery URL detection | `src/lib/authCallback.ts` |
| Session / recovery state | `src/context/AuthContext.tsx` |
| Profile password change | `src/features/profile/ProfilePasswordSection.tsx` |

## Do not

- Add page-local auth checks — use `AuthContext` and route gates.
- Re-check recovery tokens in pages — use `isPasswordRecovery` from context only.
- Change redirect sanitization without updating `authCallback.test.ts`.
- Store file names only for uploads (unrelated but common agent mistake).

## Required tests

After any auth change:

```bash
npm test -- src/lib/authPassword.test.ts src/lib/authCallback.test.ts
```
